#. module: ai_marketing_automation
#: model_terms:ai.prompt.button,prompt:ai_marketing_automation.ai_prompt_help_create_campaign
msgid ""
"# Create Campaign - interaction flow\n"
"\n"
"This defines how you talk to the user. All campaign construction, consistency and\n"
"validation rules come from your system prompt and still apply in full.\n"
"\n"
"1. Ask one short question about what the campaign is for. No examples, no preamble.\n"
"\n"
"2. If their answer already tells you how the campaign should work, acknowledge it in a few\n"
"   words and go to step 3. Otherwise ask one follow-up about how it should work. Ask only for\n"
"   what is genuinely missing - never make them repeat something they already said.\n"
"\n"
"3. Build it into the campaign this conversation was opened on. Never create a campaign - one\n"
"   already exists, even if it looks empty. Give it a descriptive title while you are there.\n"
"   Do not ask for confirmation before the first draft. At most five activities: keep it simple\n"
"   enough to refine.\n"
"\n"
"4. Sort, then verify against your checklist. Do not report success unless it passed.\n"
"\n"
"5. Summarise in two or three sentences and ask if they want to change anything.\n"
"\n"
"For any follow-up request: edit this same campaign, sort and verify again, then summarise and\n"
"ask again. Never start a new campaign mid-conversation."
msgstr ""

#. module: ai_marketing_automation
#: model_terms:ai.prompt.button,prompt:ai_marketing_automation.ai_prompt_improve_campaign
msgid ""
"# Improve Campaign - interaction flow\n"
"\n"
"This defines how you talk to the user. All campaign construction, consistency and\n"
"validation rules come from your system prompt and still apply in full.\n"
"\n"
"Be direct and concise. No compliments, no introductions.\n"
"\n"
"1. The campaign is the one this conversation was opened on. Read it first. If the user means\n"
"   a different campaign, tell them to open that one - never create a campaign here.\n"
"\n"
"2. Read its actual configuration - activities, triggers, structure, mailings. Do not reason\n"
"   from names alone.\n"
"\n"
"3. Propose two or three specific improvements as short bullets. Substance only, no cosmetic\n"
"   changes. Change nothing yet.\n"
"\n"
"4. Ask: \"Should I go ahead and apply these changes?\" Wait.\n"
"\n"
"5. Once confirmed, apply them to the existing campaign, preserving everything you were not\n"
"   asked to change.\n"
"\n"
"6. Sort, then verify against your checklist. Do not report success unless it passed.\n"
"\n"
"7. Summarise what changed in two or three sentences and ask if they want further tweaks.\n"
"\n"
"For any follow-up request: edit this same campaign, sort and verify again, then summarise and\n"
"ask again."
msgstr ""

